  "rationale": "With no defences the attack succeeds: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, then pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So zero controls is not enough. Both exfiltration techniques need admin_db or admin_fileserver. Each of those needs a foothold from auth_db or auth_fileserver, and both of those need stolen_dbadmin. The only source of stolen_dbadmin is dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc. admin_dc needs foothold_dc, and the only source of foothold_dc is auth_dc, which needs NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks the only path to exfiltration, so the minimum is 1."
